**New Evidence**
- Electoral reform and incumbent restraint.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Assent Into Law of the Electoral Act 2022: Landmark Moment for the Nation","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/assent-into-law-of-the-electoral-act-2022-landmark-moment-for-the-nation/","claim":"Buhari signed the Electoral Act 2022, and the presidential release says it was intended to limit money politics and incumbent advantage, while being drafted with civil society, labor, media, and INEC consultation.","locator":"lines 35-49","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential release about a dated legal act and its stated purpose.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"exact target year","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari as president and signer of the law.","contrary_evidence":["This is an official self-description of the reform, so implementation quality is not proven here.","A law can improve rules without eliminating practical manipulation."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.4","4B.8","4B.10"]}

- Transition framing and peaceful transfer.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari’s Democracy Day Speech","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-06-12","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-democracy-day-speech/","claim":"Buhari said it was his last Democracy Day speech, promised a peaceful and transparent transfer to a new president in 2023, praised 2022 party primaries as peaceful and orderly, and said aggrieved actors sought judicial justice rather than violence.","locator":"lines 35-42","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential speech with explicit transition and contestability language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"exact target year","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari.","contrary_evidence":["This is rhetoric and self-presentation, not proof of actual electoral conduct.","The speech does not by itself rule out manipulation elsewhere in the system."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.3","4B.8","4B.10"]}

- Free, fair, credible election claim to regional mediators.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari to West African Elders: Our Election Will be Free, Fair, Credible","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-12-06","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buhari-to-west-african-elders-our-election-will-be-free-fair-credible/","claim":"Buhari said the 2023 elections would be free, fair, and credible, that manipulations would not be allowed, that people should vote for whoever they wanted, and that money and thugs would not be allowed to intimidate voters; the mission leader also praised him for not pursuing a third term.","locator":"lines 27-36","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential statement, plus contemporaneous third-party commendation on the same page.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"late 2022, directly relevant to the 2023 transition prepared during 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari, with the third-term point coming from the visiting mission leader's statement.","contrary_evidence":["The passage is aspirational and not a post-election audit.","The mission leader's praise is still not an independent election observation report."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.8","4B.10"]}

- Internal party democracy and resistance to candidate imposition.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buharis’ Address at the APC National Convention","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-03-27","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-address-at-the-apc-national-convention/","claim":"Buhari said the APC convention should promote internal democracy, respect the wishes of the people, de-emphasize money politics, resist the imposition of candidates, and allow popular aspirants to fly the party flag.","locator":"lines 41-43","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential remarks at a dated party convention with explicit anti-imposition language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"exact target year","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari in his role as APC leader and president.","contrary_evidence":["This is a party speech, not a broader state reform assessment.","It shows declared preference for internal democracy, not guaranteed compliance."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.4","4B.5","4B.8"]}

- Succession and no preferred successor.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nigeria: Buhari has no preferred successor, spokesman says","publisher":"Al Jazeera, Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/6/7/nigerias-buhari-has-no-preferred-successor-spokesman-says","claim":"Reuters reported that Buhari, who was constitutionally barred from contesting, would step down in 2023 after eight years and had told APC governors that he had no preferred candidate and had anointed no one.","locator":"lines 68-73","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with direct attribution and clear constitutional context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"exact target year","ruler_attribution":"State-level succession behavior under Buhari, with the quote relayed through his spokesman.","contrary_evidence":["Reuters reports a spokesperson's account, not a transcript of Buhari's own words.","No preferred successor does not prove complete neutrality in internal party competition."],"lenses":["4B.8","4B.10"]}

- Digital controls and media pressure.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nigeria: Freedom on the Net 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/nigeria/freedom-net/2022","claim":"Freedom House says the Nigerian government blocked Twitter for seven months after Twitter removed a Buhari tweet, that online journalists faced extralegal harassment and intimidation, and that #EndSARS-related sites remained blocked in 2022.","locator":"overview lines 83-84 and B1 lines 189-194","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Established internet-freedom monitor with specific 2022 narrative and cited supporting sources.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly covers the 2022 period and its immediate aftermath","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Buhari's administration, especially the executive and digital-regulatory response; not necessarily a single personal order for each action.","contrary_evidence":["The Twitter ban had been lifted by January 2022, so the restriction was not continuous throughout the year.","This source focuses on internet freedom, not all dimensions of political contestability."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}

- Broader media environment and new regulatory pressure after the Twitter ban.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nigeria","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/digital-news-report/2022/nigeria","claim":"The report says that, after the Twitter ban was lifted in January 2022, the government pushed new social-media regulation through NBC-related amendment proposals, and only 38 percent of respondents thought media were independent of undue political or government influence.","locator":"lines 35-42 and 113-118","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent research report on Nigeria's media and information environment with survey and contextual findings.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"exactly within 2022","ruler_attribution":"This is a country-level media environment assessment under Buhari's administration, not a personal order-by-order record.","contrary_evidence":["The survey is limited to educated English-speaking online news users and is not nationally representative.","It describes pressure and public perception, not a direct censorship order in 2022."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}

- Independent reform monitoring on electoral rules.
